SweetSurface: refuse IOSurface wrap selectors 6/7 (S7 0244).

IOSurfaceRootUserClient selectors 6 (wrap client image) and 7 (wrap client
memory) answer with a lock result the library turns into an IOSurfaceClient.
The default case's zeroed success left a client with NULL pointers; on the
S7, once backboardd drew through the GPU, IOSurfaceGetBulkAttachments then
faulted on NULL+0x30. Refuse them: CoreAnimation takes its copying path.

diff --git a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetSurface.cpp b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetSurface.cpp
index 7f90c56..8f1182a 100644
--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetSurface.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetSurface.cpp
@@ -772,6 +772,18 @@ IOSurfaceRootUserClient::externalMethod(uint32_t selector, IOExternalMethodArgum
 		sweet_surf_log_once("sel", selector);
 		return kIOReturnSuccess;
 	}
+	case 6:         /* wrap client image: struct in 0x20 */
+	case 7:         /* wrap client memory: scalars [address, length] */
+		/*
+		 * Both answer with a lock result that the library turns into an
+		 * IOSurfaceClient. Not implemented: refuse, so the library returns
+		 * NULL and the caller (CoreAnimation's image upload) takes its
+		 * copying path. The default case's zeroed "success" left a client
+		 * with NULL pointers; on the S7 IOSurfaceGetBulkAttachments then
+		 * faulted on NULL+0x30 once backboardd drew through the GPU (S7 0244).
+		 */
+		sweet_surf_log_once("sel", selector);
+		return kIOReturnUnsupported;
 	default:
 		/* Values, notifications, ownership, timestamps...: accept and ignore. */
 		for (uint32_t i = 0; i < args->scalarOutputCount; i++) {
